        <tr><td><strong>Local Ordinance</strong></td><td>Medical marijuana ordinance passed Sept 24, 2024, 5–1 vote (per The County)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Population</strong></td><td>~6,000 (2020 Census)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>County</strong></td><td>Aroostook County (county seat)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Position</strong></td><td>I-95 terminus, opposite Woodstock, New Brunswick, Canada</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dispensaries in Houlton</h2>

    <h3>Lifted Cannabis Maine</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 32 Access Road, Houlton, ME 04730 (per liftedmaine.com/about)<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 554-6420 (per liftedmaine.com contact section)<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> 8am–6pm daily (per liftedmaine.com/about)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical only — the operator's site states "Medical Card Required, No Adult Use/Recreational." <a href="https://www.liftedmaine.com/about" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Verify directly with the operator</a>.</p>
    <p>Established in 2021, Lifted Cannabis Maine has positioned itself as a medical dispensary focused on "high quality, effective and affordable solutions for patients from Maine and beyond." Located on Houlton's Access Road near I-95, the store serves MMMP cardholders across southern Aroostook County and is the closest dispensary to the I-95 terminus at the New Brunswick border. For travelers heading north from Bangor or points south, Lifted is the natural final stop before the international crossing.</p>

    <h3>Vargas Farm</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 28 Airport Drive, Houlton, ME 04730 (per Vargas Farm Facebook page and Yelp listing)<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 405-5256 (per Vargas Farm contact information)<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Call ahead to confirm — hours not consistently published across operator sources<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical only — listed as a Medical Cannabis Dispensary on Facebook and as a Medical Cannabis Referral on Yelp.</p>
    <p>Vargas Farm operates a medical dispensary on Airport Drive in Houlton, anchored by a family cultivation operation. The store carries an in-house product line (Alignable lists "marijuana edibles, tinctures, and a variety of strains for medical use"). Mitchell Vargas runs the operation and the dispensary has built a local reputation with MMMP patients in the Houlton, Hodgdon, Linneus, and New Limerick area.</p>
  </section>

  <Callout title="September 2024 Medical Ordinance (verified: The County + WAGM)" type="insight">
    On September 24, 2024, the Houlton Town Council voted 5–1 to pass a new medical marijuana ordinance, formalizing the regulatory framework for the town's cannabis operators following a state Office of Cannabis Policy rule change. <a href="https://thecounty.me/2024/09/24/business-news/houlton-passes-new-medical-marijuana-ordinance/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The County covered the vote</a>, and <a href="https://www.wagmtv.com/2024/09/25/houlton-council-passes-new-ordinance-regarding-medical-marijuana-stores/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WAGM-TV reported it 6–1</a>. The new rules address licensing, <a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-zoning-requirements">zoning</a>, host agreements, and operational standards — bringing Houlton into line with more mature medical markets and giving existing operators a clear regulatory foundation. Council debate noted that <strong>residents had voted in 2017 to reject recreational sales</strong>, so Houlton remains a medical-only retail environment.
  </Callout>

  <section>
    <h2>Houlton's Market Context</h2>
    <p>Houlton is the southernmost stop on I-95 in Maine and the seat of Aroostook County — the largest U.S. county east of the Mississippi. The town sits on the international border opposite Woodstock, New Brunswick, and the Houlton–Woodstock border crossing is a major node for cross-border traffic. For cannabis, the border location gives Houlton a distinctive mix: year-round Aroostook County patients, I-95 travelers, and cross-border visitors from New Brunswick.</p>
    <p>Houlton's retail framework is <strong>medical only</strong>. Per the <a href="https://thecounty.me/2024/08/27/business-news/houlton-introduces-new-marijuana-ordinance/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">August 2024 The County reporting</a>, residents voted in 2017 to not allow recreational sales, and the September 2024 ordinance reinforced that posture. Lifted Cannabis Maine and Vargas Farm both serve MMMP cardholders and both describe themselves as medical-only on their operator pages. For shoppers seeking a full adult-use menu, Presque Isle is ~60 mi north on I-95.</p>
    <p>For operators, Houlton functions as the I-95 anchor for southern Aroostook and the medical hub for the border region. Any operator considering a Houlton expansion should note the voter posture — adult-use retail is not currently on the table per the public record.</p>
  </section>

